Chapter 40: The Blight-Tusk Core
The deep interior of Outpost Rift #42 narrowed into an ancient, subterranean cavern of jagged obsidian stalagmites.
While Renna, Tobias, and Mina safely cleared the three remaining Stalkers in the upper ravine, Kaelen moved silently through the cavern tunnels under the cover of [Phantom Kinetic Cloak].
At the center of the cavern sat the Rift Core—a pulsing, three-meter crystal of unstable void energy embedded in the bedrock. Guarding it was the rift’s apex predator: a Blight-Tusk Behemoth (Tier-B Elite).
The monster stood twelve feet high at the shoulder, its massive frame covered in thick, dark-green chitin plating and matted bristles. Two massive, four-foot serrated tusks jutted from its lower jaw, dripping with corrosive acid that hissed as it touched the stone floor.
[Target Identified: Blight-Tusk Behemoth (Tier-B Elite)]
 * Attributes: High-Density Chitin Armor, Acidic Tusk Thruster, Heavy Seismic Stomp.
 * Threat Assessment: High. High physical defense and kinetic momentum.
Kaelen stepped out of the shadow of a stalagmite, dropping his cloaking shroud.
The Behemoth’s glowing red eyes locked onto Kaelen instantly. It let out a deafening, gut-wrenching roar that shook dust from the cavern ceiling, scraping its massive front hooves against the obsidian floor before igniting a burst of acidic steam from its nostrils.
THUD! THUD! THUD!
The four-ton monster surged forward in a terrifying, high-velocity charge, its massive serrated tusks aimed directly at Kaelen’s chest.
Kaelen didn't evade. He didn't use [Void-Step].
He wanted to test the limits of his newly forged [Hydra's Void-Scale Harness].
He planted both boots into the cavern floor, locking his skeletal framework with [Terrestrial Anchor] and engaging his Anchor-Greaves.
He crossed his arms over his chest, bracing his forearms—protected by his Kinetic-Void Bracers—directly against the incoming impact.
BOOOOOOOOOOM!
The four-ton Behemoth slammed into Kaelen with the momentum of a runaway freight train. The serrated tusks struck his chest with crushing, armor-shattering force.
ZZZZZZT!
The invisible Hydra's Void-Scale Harness beneath his uniform ignited with a dark purple pulse.
Forty percent of the crushing kinetic impact was instantly dissipated across the flexible scale-mesh, while Kaelen’s sub-dermal [Obsidian Hard-Plating] and [Abyssal Shell Resonance] absorbed the rest. The acidic coating melted Kaelen's cheap outer utility vest, but dissolved instantly upon contact with his [Corrosive Blood Coating]-reinforced skin.
Kaelen slid back three inches through the stone floor—and stopped dead.
The Behemoth’s glowing eyes widened in sheer, mammalian shock. Its full-speed charge had failed to break a single bone in the small human standing before it.
"My turn," Kaelen said coldly.
Moving with his base 102 Agility, Kaelen uncrossed his arms and grabbed both of the monster's four-foot tusks with his bare hands.
He channeled his 101 Strength.
CRACK!
With a brutal, violent wrench of his upper body, Kaelen snapped both massive tusks off at the root.
The Behemoth shrieked in agony, but Kaelen was already in the air.
He activated [Lightning-Phase Blitz].
ZAP-BOOM!
Coated in high-density blue lightning, Kaelen delivered a three-hit kinetic barrage straight into the Behemoth's exposed neck joint.
BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!
The concussive, electric-boosted shockwave shattered the creature's spine and tore through its central mana core. The twelve-foot Behemoth shuddered violently before collapsing onto its side, dead.
Kaelen pressed both bare palms onto the massive carcass.
"[Dissect & Assimilate]!"
Dark gray vapor erupted, devouring the four-ton Behemoth in seconds.
[Deconstructing Blight-Tusk Behemoth (Tier-B Elite)...]
[Mass Assimilation Complete!]
