Kaelen exhaled a hot mist of purified energy.
His Strength and Agility were now past 110 points, while his Vitality crossed the 100-point threshold. His physical vessel felt lighter, denser, and practically indestructible.
He quickly picked up the glowing Rift Core Crystal, along with the broken tusk catalysts, and stored them inside his spatial salvage pouch. He would not run off to the Black Market to sell them yet; he intended to hoard his loot until his stash grew massive enough to warrant a multi-million-credit transaction.
Kaelen pulled off the ruined, acid-singed remnants of his outer utility vest, throwing them into the cavern lava pool. Underneath, his Hydra's Void-Scale Harness and uniform remained completely pristine.
He pulled a spare, slightly worn utility vest from his spatial pouch, slouched his shoulders, and put on his timid, pale expression.
Holding a broken, low-grade Tier-C Stalker claw in his hand, Kaelen trotted out of the cavern system and back into the foggy ravine.
Renna, Tobias, and Mina were standing near the ravine exit, breathing heavily over the corpses of the three Stalkers they had just defeated together.
"Kaelen!" Renna yelled, turning around with her shield raised, her eyes lighting up with relief as she saw him shuffling out of the mist. "Are you okay?!"
"I... I hid behind a big rock inside a pipe, Renna!" Kaelen stammered meekly, holding up the broken Stalker claw with trembling hands. "I found this claw on the ground... did... did we win?"
Tobias let out a breathless laugh, slinging his crossbow over his shoulder. "We won, buddy! We held the whole western flank!"
Renna smiled warmly, patting Kaelen's shoulder. "Good job staying hidden, Kaelen. Let's head back to the extraction point."
As Squad 4 walked toward the rift exit, Kaelen fell three paces behind them, his slouched posture hiding the Level 15 power humming beneath his skin.
The rift was cleared, Ironclad had fled in terror, and his squad was safe. The long game was proceeding perfectly.
